---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import NewsletterEmbed from '../../components/NewsletterEmbed.astro';



const articleStyles = `
    .article-body a {
        color: var(--accent);
        text-decoration: underline;
        text-underline-offset: 2px;
        text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
        transition: color var(--duration-short) ease;
    }
    .article-body a:hover { color: var(--text); }
    .article-body ul {
        margin: 0 0 20px;
        padding-left: 22px;
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        list-style: disc;
    }
    .article-body li {
        font-size: 16px;
        line-height: 1.75;
        margin-bottom: 8px;
    }
    .article-body strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 600; }
    .article-body .endmatter {
        margin-top: 56px;
        padding-top: 28px;
        border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .article-body .endmatter-label {
        font-size: 11px;
        letter-spacing: 0.09em;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
        margin: 0 0 14px;
    }
    .article-body .endmatter ul {
        margin: 0;
        padding-left: 18px;
        list-style: none;
    }
    .article-body .endmatter li {
        position: relative;
        font-size: 13.5px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
        margin-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .article-body .endmatter li::before {
        content: "";
        position: absolute;
        left: -18px;
        top: 9px;
        width: 5px;
        height: 1px;
        background: var(--text-tertiary);
    }
    .article-body .endmatter li:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .article-body .disclaimer {
        margin-top: 24px;
        padding: 16px 18px;
        background: var(--bg-subtle);
        border-radius: var(--radius-md);
        font-size: 13px;
        line-height: 1.65;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
    }
    .article-body .note {
        font-size: 14px;
        line-height: 1.6;
        color: var(--text-tertiary);
    }
`;
---
<ArticleLayout
    title="Why I stopped retatrutide after two weeks."
    description="4.2 kg in two weeks, plenty of energy, and data heading the wrong way."
    ogUrl="https://maxguerois.com/newsletter/arreter-le-reta"
    ogImage="https://maxguerois.com/health-journey/blog/arreter-reta-cover.jpg"
    articleStyles={articleStyles}
>

<div class="container">
    <a href="/newsletter" class="back">← Back to the newsletter</a>

    <div class="article-meta">30 August 2026</div>
    <h1 class="article-title">Why I stopped retatrutide after two weeks.</h1>
    <p class="article-subtitle">4.2 kg in two weeks, plenty of energy, and data heading the wrong way.</p>

    <img
        class="article-img"
        src="/health-journey/blog/arreter-reta-cover.jpg"
        alt="Max Guerois training, holding a weight plate"
        fetchpriority="high"
    >

    <div class="article-body">
        <p>J'ai perdu <strong>4,2 kg en deux semaines</strong> sous rétatrutide.</p>

        <p>Then I stopped.</p>

        <p>Not because of the cost. Not because I could not stick with it. Because my data was heading the wrong way.</p>

        <h2 class="section-heading">When retatrutide works, you feel it fast</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>moins de <em>food noise</em></li>
            <li>very fast weight loss</li>
        </ul>

        <p>And for me, more <strong>focus</strong>.</p>

        <p>Probably because I had fewer blood-sugar crashes.</p>

        <p>In training, I had energy.</p>

        <p>I ate less, but I ate.</p>

        <p>The disaster story you read everywhere, I did not live it.</p>

        <h2 class="section-heading">On reta, resting heart rate can climb</h2>

        <p>It is in the phase 2 trial, in the <em>New England Journal of Medicine</em>.</p>

        <p>The rise is dose-dependent. At 8 and 12 mg weekly: <strong>5 to 7 beats per minute</strong>.</p>

        <p>Two honest caveats.</p>

        <p>It peaks at week 24, then it declines.</p>

        <p>And in that trial it was not associated with any cardiovascular event.</p>

        <p>For scale: tirzepatide rises 1 to 3 bpm. Semaglutide, 1 to 4.</p>

        <p>Retatrutide does more. That is the price of a triple agonist.</p>

        <img
            class="article-img"
            src="/health-journey/blog/arreter-reta-heartrate.jpg"
            alt="A 30-day resting heart rate chart"
            loading="lazy"
        >

        <p><strong>Bryan Johnson stopped his microdosing for the same reason.</strong></p>

        <p>Three weeks. Resting heart rate +3 bpm, variability &minus;7, sleep &minus;10%.</p>

        <p>The most obsessive man in longevity stops on numbers, not on a feeling.</p>

        <h2 class="section-heading">The 2nd side effect: losing muscle</h2>

        <p>Part of the weight lost is not fat. It is <strong>lean mass</strong>.</p>

        <p>So muscle.</p>

        <p>Estimates vary, but the range is wide: <strong>between a quarter and 40%</strong> of the weight lost.</p>

        <p>STEP 1 and SUSTAIN 8 reach 39-40%. Other meta-analyses land around 25%.</p>

        <p>A word on what you cannot measure yourself.</p>

        <p>Smart scales <strong>infer</strong> body composition. They do not measure it.</p>

        <p>Reliable on weight. Not reliable enough on composition.</p>

        <p>So nobody, me included, can claim a muscle-loss figure from a scale.</p>

        <h2 class="section-heading">4 priorities if you use reta</h2>

        <ul>
            <li>a genuinely <strong>data-driven</strong> approach: a watch or a band, to track how your numbers move</li>
            <li>at least <strong>1.2 g of protein</strong> per kilo per day</li>
            <li><strong>2 to 4 strength sessions</strong> a week</li>
            <li>real sleep: regular, calm, no coffee late</li>
        </ul>

        <img
            class="article-img"
            src="/health-journey/blog/arreter-reta-breakfast.jpg"
            alt="A breakfast plate: berries, nuts, avocado"
            loading="lazy"
        >

        <p>I stopped after two weeks because my numbers were getting worse.</p>

        <p>Not the cost. Not willpower. Data.</p>

        <p>Until the next edition, take care.</p>

        <div style="margin: var(--sp-12) 0;">
            <NewsletterEmbed />
        </div>

        <div class="endmatter">
        <p class="endmatter-label">Sources</p>
            <ul>
            <li>Jastreboff et al., <em>New England Journal of Medicine</em>, 2023 : retatrutide phase 2 trial, dose-dependent rise in resting heart rate, peaking at week 24 then declining. <a href="https://www.nejm.org/doi/full/10.1056/NEJMoa2301972" target="_blank" rel="noopener">NEJMoa2301972</a></li>
            <li>Smart scales and body composition: reliable on weight, not on composition. <em>JMIR mHealth</em>, 2021. <a href="https://mhealth.jmir.org/2021/4/e22487/citations" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DOI 10.2196/22487</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="disclaimer">Personal experimentation, not medical advice. Retatrutide is not an approved medicine in Europe. Talk to a doctor.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</ArticleLayout>
